    <item>
      <title>11.8. Decluttering codes from View Controller (Recommended Read)</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/05-networking-and-apis/working-with-json/useful-extra-11.8.-decluttering-codes-from-view-controller/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/05-networking-and-apis/working-with-json/useful-extra-11.8.-decluttering-codes-from-view-controller/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;118-decluttering-codes-from-view-controller-recommended-read&#34;&gt;11.8. Decluttering codes from View Controller (Recommended Read)&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#118-decluttering-codes-from-view-controller-recommended-read&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If you noticed, we have 281 lines of code in ViewController.swift. It appears to be a jumble of code. And in many ways, it&amp;rsquo;s hard to read when you&amp;rsquo;ll return to it after a week.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We can utilize protocols and extensions to break the code into multiple files, making it more modular.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;separating-the-api-calls-from-the-controller&#34;&gt;Separating the API calls from the Controller&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#separating-the-api-calls-from-the-controller&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s first separate the code we used to call the Contacts API. The methods we have related to the Contacts API are:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title></title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/05-networking-and-apis/working-with-json/11.2.-app11-getting-all-the-contact-names-getall-endpoint/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/05-networking-and-apis/working-with-json/11.2.-app11-getting-all-the-contact-names-getall-endpoint/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;112-app11-getting-all-the-contact-names-getall-endpoint&#34;&gt;11.2. App11: Getting All the Contact Names (getall endpoint)&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#112-app11-getting-all-the-contact-names-getall-endpoint&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;representing-json-in-swift-getall&#34;&gt;Representing JSON in Swift (getall)&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#representing-json-in-swift-getall&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;From the API details (&lt;a href=&#34;11.1.-the-json-api-for-the-contact-app.md&#34; title=&#34;mention&#34;&gt;11.1.-the-json-api-for-the-contact-app.md&lt;/a&gt;), we know that &lt;code&gt;getall&lt;/code&gt; API returns a JSON string like:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-json&#34; data-lang=&#34;json&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;{&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;contacts&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: [&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;            &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;name&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;David Tu&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        },&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;            &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;name&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Alice Smith&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    ]&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Now, think about the structure of the JSON above.&lt;/strong&gt; First of all, the whole thing is a JSON object.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;This JSON object contains a JSON array named &amp;ldquo;contacts.&amp;rdquo;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The &amp;ldquo;contacts&amp;rdquo; array contains a list of two JSON objects.&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Each JSON object contains a key-value pair, where the key is &amp;ldquo;name.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Now, think about a similar struct/class in Swift. Can we represent the above JSON structure with a Swift struct?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
  </channel>
